{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/matharium/status/2108693741280403537","id":"2108693741280403537","text":"A Chladni plate is a square plate driven at one frequency, with sand on top.\n\nIn mode (n, m) it moves as u = cos(nπx)cos(mπy) ± cos(mπx)cos(nπy). Each grain is kicked in proportion to |u|, so it wanders until it reaches a line where u = 0. Bending waves on a plate have ω ∝ k², so the note rises as n² + m²: 135 Hz for (1, 2), 918 Hz for (3, 5).\n\nChladni published the figures in 1787; Sophie Germain's theory of them won the Paris prize in 1816.","raw_text":{"text":"A Chladni plate is a square plate driven at one frequency, with sand on top.\n\nIn mode (n, m) it moves as u = cos(nπx)cos(mπy) ± cos(mπx)cos(nπy). Each grain is kicked in proportion to |u|, so it wanders until it reaches a line where u = 0. Bending waves on a plate have ω ∝ k², so the note rises as n² + m²: 135 Hz for (1, 2), 918 Hz for (3, 5).\n\nChladni published the figures in 1787; Sophie Germain's theory of them won the Paris prize in 1816.","display_text_range":[0,446],"facets":[{"type":"media","indices":[278,301],"id":"2108618197650051072","display":"pic.x.com/XzYEdGuZW8","original":"https://t.co/XzYEdGuZW8","replacement":"https://x.com/matharium/status/2108693741280403537/video/1"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"matharium","url":"https://x.com/matharium","id":"1475728988949516288","followers":9163,"following":977,"likes":351,"media_count":378,"name":"matharium","description":"Math was never the problem. The explanation was.","raw_description":{"text":"Math was never the problem. The explanation was.","facets":[]},"location":"","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1475728988949516288/1783458915","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2074601031233839104/HCl-U9nQ_200x200.jpg","joined":"Tue Dec 28 07:23:25 +0000 2021","protected":false,"website":{"url":"https://linktr.ee/matharium","display_url":"linktr.ee/matharium"},"verification":{"verified":tr